## Control {{controlId}}: Employ Least Privilege for Security Functions

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization employs the principle of least privilege, including for specific security functions and privileged accounts, within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant. Least privilege is enforced through Azure AD Privileged Identity Management (PIM) with just-in-time access, role eligibility assignments, and approval workflows that ensure users operate with minimum necessary permissions.

{{#if pimConfigured}}
Azure AD Privileged Identity Management enforces least privilege through {{roleEligibilityCount}} just-in-time role eligibilities. Administrators are assigned eligible roles rather than permanent active assignments, requiring explicit activation with time-bound elevation (maximum 8 hours per activation). Each activation requires business justification and approval from a designated approver before privileged access is granted.
{{else}}
Azure AD Privileged Identity Management has not been configured. Least privilege enforcement relies on static role assignments pending PIM implementation.
{{/if}}

{{#if directoryRolesConfigured}}
Directory roles are scoped to {{directoryRolesCount}} distinct security functions, each granting only the permissions necessary for the assigned function. Role assignments follow the principle of least functionality, with administrative units further restricting scope where applicable.
{{/if}}

{{#if infraResources}}
Supporting infrastructure:
{{#each infraResources}}
- {{resourceType}} "{{name}}"{{#if properties.retention_days}} (retention: {{properties.retention_days}} days){{/if}}
{{/each}}
{{/if}}

**Responsible Party:** {{variables.accessControlAdministrator}}

**Verification Method:** Review PIM role eligibility assignments, activation logs with justifications, and approval workflow records. Verify no permanent active assignments for privileged roles.

